---
// PROTOTYPE: how the situation report is made. The source catalogue is generated from
// data/catalogue/sources.yaml (via the build's catalogue.json), never written by hand.
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import catalogue from "../data/catalogue.json";
import { formatDate, ordinal } from "../lib/proceedings";
import { asOf, RULE, TERMS, totals } from "../lib/tracker";

type Source = {
  id: string; name: string; publisher: string; url: string; description: string; kind: string; arenas: string[];
  access: string; status: string; reason: string | null; paywalled: boolean;
  terms: { licence: string | null; url: string | null; verified: string | null };
};
const sources = catalogue as Source[];
const LEVELS: Record<string, string> = { international: "International", eu: "European Union", domestic: "Germany" };
const ORDER = ["international", "eu", "domestic"];
const levels = (s: Source) => ORDER.filter((l) => s.arenas.includes(l)).map((l) => LEVELS[l]).join(", ");
// DIP is partly ingested already; the catalogue marks it planned until the full pull lands.
const statusOf = (s: Source) => (s.id === "dip" ? "In use" : s.status === "planned" ? "Planned" : s.status === "ingested" ? "In use" : "Referenced");
const rank = (s: Source) => ["In use", "Planned"].indexOf(statusOf(s));
const used = sources.filter((s) => s.status !== "referenced").sort((a, b) => rank(a) - rank(b) || a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
const pointedTo = sources.filter((s) => s.status === "referenced").sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
const terms = (s: Source) => (s.terms.verified ? s.terms.licence ?? "Checked" : "Being checked");
---
<Site title="Method and sources | Germany on AI" description="How the situation report on German AI policy is made: what counts as AI, where the data comes from, and its limits.">
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>Method and sources</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every figure in the situation report is counted from public records by a rule stated on this page,
      and every item links to its source. Rebuilding the report from the same records gives the same numbers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-counts">
    <h2><a class="self" href="#what-counts">What counts as AI</a></h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A parliamentary proceeding counts as AI-related if {RULE}.</p>
      <p>
        The Bundestag's documentalists index every proceeding with keywords from a controlled thesaurus.
        The title rule catches recent items they have not indexed yet. Some proceedings meet the rule while
        touching AI only in part, such as a broad digital-policy bill. A documented labelling step will
        replace this rule later.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="coverage">
    <h2><a class="self" href="#coverage">Period covered</a></h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Every electoral term from the {ordinal(TERMS[0].term)} Bundestag, which convened on {formatDate(TERMS[0].start)}. That term
        saw the federal AI strategy (November 2018) and the Bundestag's Enquete Commission on Artificial
        Intelligence. Whole terms are used because parliament organises its records by term. The report
        focuses on the current term; earlier terms are shown as context. {totals.all.toLocaleString("en")} AI proceedings in all,
        up to {formatDate(asOf)}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="dates">
    <h2><a class="self" href="#dates">Dates and the timeline</a></h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Parliament's documentation system dates a proceeding by its most recent document, not by when it
        began. Counts per quarter and timeline entries use that date, so a proceeding that started earlier
        appears when it last moved.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the timeline, an event known only to a month, a season or a year is a bar over that period.
        Government, EU and international events come from research notes for now and are marked "Source not
        yet linked" until their own sources are added.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="limits">
    <h2><a class="self" href="#limits">Known limits</a></h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul>
        <li>Written and oral questions are filed by individual members; until speeches and questions are loaded, they are not attributed to a parliamentary group.</li>
        <li>Live data so far covers parliament only. Government, EU and international sources are being added.</li>
        <li>A bill and a written question each count once, so the counts measure activity.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="catalogue">
    <h2><a class="self" href="#catalogue">Sources</a></h2>
    <p class="note">The report quotes third-party text briefly and links to it. Each source's terms of use are recorded below.</p>

    <h3 id="catalogue-used">Data sources</h3>
    <table class="catalogue">
      <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Level</th><th>Status</th><th>Terms</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {used.map((s) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="external noopener">{s.name}</a><span class="pub">{s.publisher}</span></td>
            <td>{levels(s)}</td>
            <td>{statusOf(s)}</td>
            <td>{s.terms.url ? <a href={s.terms.url} target="_blank" rel="external noopener">{terms(s)}</a> : terms(s)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 id="catalogue-others">Other trackers, research and reporting</h3>
    <p class="note">Others who track parts of this ground. Their work is not part of the data, but it is worth reading alongside.</p>
    <table class="catalogue">
      <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Level</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {pointedTo.map((s) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="external noopener">{s.name}</a><span class="pub">{s.publisher}</span></td>
            <td>{levels(s)}</td>
            <td>{s.description}{s.paywalled ? " Subscription required." : ""}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</Site>

<style>
  h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 26px 0 8px; }
  .catalogue { width: 100%; max-width: 60rem; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14px; }
  .catalogue th { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; padding: 6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  .catalogue td { padding: 9px 12px 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
  .catalogue td:first-child { width: 38%; }
  .catalogue td:first-child a { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); text-decoration-color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .pub { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .catalogue th:nth-child(2), .catalogue td:nth-child(2) { display: none; } }
</style>
